<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- The C-27J Spartan's upgrades (docs/development/vehicle-c27j.md, "The upgrade tree"): the defensive aids, which stand alone, and the
       three hold fits (D'thorga Vehicles 0.128.0), either/or with each other because each fills the hold: stretchers, the MC-27J gun kit
       and the fire-fighting tank. Each fit's weight is carried mass, taking cargo room (owner, 19 Nov 2026: "weight counts like cargo");
       the weights are authored. Node keys are saved in the game: never rename or remove one. Not yet tested in game. -->
  <Vehicles.UpgradeTreeDef>
    <defName>Phobos_C27J_UpgradeTree</defName>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosUpgradeCostsLikeTunes" />
    </modExtensions>
    <nodes>
    <li>
      <!-- The RAAF's self-protection suite [P4]: the missile warning receiver built into its avionics cues turrets that blind heat-seeking
           missiles, as the Osprey's infrared jammer, and chaff and flare dispensers fed from a magazine haulers top up (the owner's card of
           26 Nov 2026: per aircraft; Framework 0.316.0's Phobos_Countermeasures). Its draw, 40 A, is authored, in its loadout. Its own icon since
           D'thorga Vehicles 0.127.0, and its pods on both gear fairings since 0.127.1 (the owner's picks of 26 Nov 2026). -->
      <key>DefensiveAids</key>
      <label>Defensive aids</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A self-protection set cued by the missile warning receiver: turrets that blind heat-seeking missiles, and dispensers that fire chaff and flares from a magazine haulers keep topped up. Air defences hit far less often and lock on more slowly; the turrets draw power while the engines run.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/C27J/Upgrades/DefensiveAids</icon>
      <work>3500</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(2, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>PhobosResearch_OspreyInfraredJammer</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_InfraredJammer</def>
              <value>1</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_Countermeasures</def>
              <value>1</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <!-- Its flight computer comes from its parts bill (Bill_C27J.xml): the turrets are what is left, as the Osprey's jammer. -->
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>20</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
        <ComponentSpacer>1</ComponentSpacer>
      </ingredients>
      <!-- A pod on each main-gear fairing, on the body's canvas (assets/phobos-vehicles/export_c27j.py; agent placement). -->
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/C27J/C27J_DefensiveAids</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(34, 27)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- 36 stretchers in the hold [P1], carried as the litter kit's are (D'thorga Framework 0.329.0's Phobos_Litters): downed people lie
           on them and anyone in the crew who can doctor tends them. Stanchions and stretchers, 360 kg [A]. Its icon is the litter kit's:
           the same stretchers. -->
      <key>Stretchers</key>
      <label>Stretchers</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>Stanchions and 36 stretchers along the hold: an air ambulance. Downed people are carried lying down, and anyone in the crew who can doctor tends them. Fills the hold: either this, the gun kit or the fire-fighting tank.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Fittings/LitterKit</icon>
      <work>2500</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(7, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>PhobosResearch_C27J</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
        <li>GunKit</li>
        <li>FireTank</li>
      </disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_Litters</def>
              <value>36</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>CargoCapacity</def>
              <value>-360</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_KitKilograms</def>
              <value>360</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
        <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosSystemsUpgrade" />
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>60</Steel>
        <Cloth>80</Cloth>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- A roll-on fire-fighting tank of 7,950 L [P1] (D'thorga Framework 0.329.0's CompPhobosFireTank and Phobos_FireTankLitres): a
           colonist pumps it full from open water beside the parked aircraft (the owner's card of 26 Nov 2026), and a water drop pass empties
           it along a line, putting out the fires beneath. The tank empty, 2,000 kg [A]; its water is weighed as it is pumped in, a kilogram
           a litre. Its pipe out of the left jump door is the owner's pick. -->
      <key>FireTank</key>
      <label>Fire-fighting tank</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A roll-on tank of 7,950 litres with its discharge pipe out of the left door. Pumped full from open water on the ground, it empties along a water drop pass, putting out the fires beneath; full, it weighs nearly eight tonnes more. Fills the hold: either this, the stretchers or the gun kit.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/C27J/Upgrades/FireTank</icon>
      <work>3000</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(12, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>PhobosResearch_C27J</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
        <li>Stretchers</li>
        <li>GunKit</li>
      </disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_FireTankLitres</def>
              <value>7950</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>CargoCapacity</def>
              <value>-2000</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_KitKilograms</def>
              <value>2000</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
        <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosSystemsUpgrade" />
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>150</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>4</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/C27J/C27J_FireTank</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(34, 27)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Leonardo's MC-27J gun kit [S]: a 30 mm cannon on a roll-on pallet firing out of the left jump door (Turrets_C27J.xml). The
           loadmaster works it; its side-gun marker turns the aircraft's circles left, so the gun faces the centre (the owner's card of 26 Nov
           2026). Its arc is the left side, 60 degrees either way of straight out [A]. It stops with the aft hold it is mounted in [A]. The
           pallet, the gun and its rounds, 1,000 kg [A]. Its barrel is the owner's pick of the slim one. -->
      <key>GunKit</key>
      <label>MC-27J gun kit</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A 30 mm cannon on a roll-on pallet, firing out of the left door, worked by the loadmaster. Told to circle a point, the aircraft turns left so the gun faces the centre and fires on what is inside the circle. Fills the hold: either this, the stretchers or the fire-fighting tank.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/C27J/Upgrades/GunKit</icon>
      <work>3000</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(29, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>PhobosResearch_OspreyRampGun</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
        <li>Stretchers</li>
        <li>FireTank</li>
      </disableIfUpgradeNodesEnabled>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.VehicleUpgrade">
          <roles>
            <li>
              <key>loadmaster</key>
              <editKey>gunKit</editKey>
              <handlingTypes>Turret</handlingTypes>
              <slotsToOperate>1</slotsToOperate>
              <turretIds>
                <li>GunKit</li>
              </turretIds>
            </li>
          </roles>
        </li>
        <li Class="Vehicles.TurretUpgrade">
          <turrets>
            <li>
              <key>GunKit</key>
              <def>Phobos_C27J_GunKit</def>
              <gizmoLabel>Side gun</gizmoLabel>
              <component>
                <key>AftHold</key>
                <healthPercent>0</healthPercent>
              </component>
              <angleRestricted>(210, 330)</angleRestricted>
              <defaultAngleRotated>270</defaultAngleRotated>
              <renderProperties>
                <north>(-1.86, -4.21)</north>
              </renderProperties>
            </li>
          </turrets>
        </li>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>CargoCapacity</def>
              <value>-1000</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_KitKilograms</def>
              <value>1000</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
        <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosSystemsUpgrade" />
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>120</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>6</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </li>
    </nodes>
  </Vehicles.UpgradeTreeDef>
</Defs>
